OL,3,AHealey risks breaking minimum wage
OL,4,Apromise for younger workers
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe Chancellor, John Healey, has
OL,7,Fsuggested that younger workers might
OL,8,Fnot receive the same minimum wage as
OL,9,Fothers before the next election,
OL,10,Fpotentially breaking a Labour manifesto
OL,11,Fpromise.
OL,13,FIn 2024, Labour said it would remove
OL,14,F"discriminatory age bands", vowing to
OL,15,Fend the gap between the adult minimum
OL,16,Fwage and pay for 18 to 20-year-olds.
OL,18,FBut in last week's Budget, Healey said
OL,19,Fthat younger workers would see the same
OL,20,Fincrease as older workers, leaving a
OL,21,Fgap between the two rates this year.
OL,23,APub: 31-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG3/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
